From ec746e5f922c541a4bf9914d3aa941be6537114c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:08:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(verify): hole-wall excuse credits tessellation only,
 not a polygon's flats

The containment kinds' solid law excused a hole-wall facet by its full
chord dip into the swept disc, so a coarse polygon hole's flats (an
octagon's dip ~0.4-0.7 mm) passed a gouge silently. chord_dip now
credits at most HOLE_CHORD_CREDIT = DEV_TOL (0.01 mm), the mesh
tolerance a round wall's tessellation stands within; a deeper dip is
real material and convicts.

Pinned by hole_wall_chord: octagon and 16-gon holes cut to their corner
circle by a drill, a bore orbit and a thread helix convict; a 96-gon
round hole stays clean for all three.

Fixes #1217

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
