From 4ec973a08c036875125bd597d08c04cd2f52f897 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:29:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(verify): a polygon declared at its corner circle
 earns no full rim credit

A facet edge on a declared hole rim is excused its whole chord dip only
when it dips at most RIM_SAG_MAX (0.05 mm) inside that circle - a round
wall's tessellation. A deeper chord is a polygon's flat and gets the
0.01 mm mesh credit like every off-rim edge, so a drill, bore or thread
of an octagon's corner-circle size convicts on its flats.

Fixes #1231

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
